> [what to wish for?]

How about a nice big stack of silver daggers? you want at least 10, I
reckon. They're very handy, and a bugger to acquire through polypiling.
My last game I shuddered something in the region of a thousand arrows
(in stacks of 5 or less) to yield only about 4 silver daggers.

Otherwise, start wishing up other ppls' quest artifacts: something with
spare MR would be nice, or one of the 'half physical damage' ones.

And 3 magic markers ain't that much: You can always use more- I mean,
when you've got 30 or 40 silver dragon hides kicking about, the chances
of getting at least one of them past +5 are pretty good, but it takes a
*lot* of scrolls. Same with daggers- I mean +7 is nice and all, but why
settle when you can try to push some of the spares to +8 or +9 or even
further? Then there's all the reverse genocide scrolls you'll be
wanting - there's probably 3 markers' worth there alone.

Of course, in a way the whole thread is redundant. An extinctionist
doesn't *need* to wish for anything. He just has to be patient. Sooner
or later, whatever it is you want will drop at your feet in a gory pool
of monster innards.



